-- title:
--   Injectivity of expansion along a substitution over a local ring
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative noetherian local ring, with residue map $\mathrm{residue} : B \to k$ onto its residue field $k$, and let $n, d$ be natural numbers. Let $\rho : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]$ be a family of multivariate formal power series each of whose constant coefficients vanishes, so that substitution of $\rho$ is defined, and let $b : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]$ be a further family. Assume given a basis $\beta$, indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d$, of the $k$-vector space $k[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!] / I$, where $I$ is the ideal generated by the set of coefficientwise reductions $\mathrm{map}(\mathrm{residue}\,B)(\rho_i)$, and assume that for each $j$ the basis vector $\beta_j$ is the class modulo $I$ of the reduction of $b_j$. Then for all families $c, c' : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]$, the equality $\sum_j \mathrm{subst}_{\rho}(c_j)\, b_j = \sum_j \mathrm{subst}_{\rho}(c'_j)\, b_j$ in $B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]$ forces $c = c'$; that is, the map $c \mapsto \sum_j c_j(\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)\, b_j$ is injective.
--
--   This is the injectivity, or uniqueness, half of the statement that $B[\![x]\!]$ is free of rank $d$ over itself via substitution by $\rho$ with basis $b_1,\dots,b_d$, the existence half being the assertion that every power series admits such an expansion; the hypothesis on $\beta$ records that the reductions of the $b_j$ form a $k$-basis of the fibre $k[\![x]\!]/(\bar\rho_1,\dots,\bar\rho_n)$. It feeds the any-lift form of that freeness result, [`MvPowerSeries.existsUnique_eq_sum_subst_mul_of_basis_residueField_tensor_quotient`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.existsUnique_eq_sum_subst_mul_of_basis_residueField_tensor_quotient), and the uniqueness statement for substitutions used in the formal theory of $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules; over a field the corresponding finiteness, flatness and existence of a basis are supplied by [`MvPowerSeries.finite_flat_exists_basis_substAlgHom_of_finite_quotient`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.finite_flat_exists_basis_substAlgHom_of_finite_quotient).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_eq_of_sum_subst_mul_eq_of_basis_quotient_map_residue.lean

